[[File:S1E17 Young Zhalia Gareon Klaus.png|thumb|170px|Young Zhalia receives [[Gareon]] from [[Klaus]]]]
Zhalia Moon was an orphan living in the streets. She could barely find anything to eat and was bullied by other kids. Until she was adopted by [[Klaus]], an evil [[Organization]] scientist, who saw something in her. Offered power and a place to belong, she was trained in espionage as an Organization agent. She was given the [[Amulet]] of [[Gareon]], and the two quickly bonded. {{source|The Vampire Loses Its Fangs}}

[[File:S1E11 Young Zhalia Flashback.png|thumb|170px|A teenage Zhalia gets bullied by thugs]]
As an Organization operative, she was sent as a spy to infiltrate the [[Huntik Foundation]]. Originally a rival, she became a member of [[Dante Vale]]'s team alongside [[Lok Lambert]], [[Sophie Casterwill]], and [[Cherit]]. {{source|Words of Truth, Heart of Lies}} She did, however, sustain a bitter relationship with Sophie.
<!--- Details of adventures with the Foundation need to be added --->

Through her time with the Foundation, she found unexpected friends in both Lok and Dante but was still loyal to Klaus, the one man whom she considered to be a father figure. Turning on her new friends in the [[castle of Vlad Dracul]] under Klaus' instructions, Zhalia found herself unable to finish off those whom she considered to be her friends. Though she joined Dante instead of attacking him, Dante was still defeated by Klaus. In a last-ditch effort, Zhalia invoked [[King Basilisk]], using its power to turn Klaus into stone. After the battle, Zhalia decided to leave the team, ashamed of what she had done. {{source|The Vampire Loses Its Fangs}}
<!--- Details of adventures with the Foundation need to be added --->

Zhalia continued to feel guilty over her betrayal and decided to help them claim the [[Legendary Titan]] of Body, [[Behemoth]], After posing as an Amazon who wanted leadership of the tribe, she gained possession of the Amulet and gave it to Dante. This marked her rejoining the Huntik team. {{Source|Ladies' Choice}}
<!--- Details of adventures with the Foundation need to be added --->

When captured by [[the Professor]], himself, Zhalia claimed herself to be Vensetta Qew, an operative for the Organization.  {{source|To Be Together}}

<!--- Details of adventures with the Foundation need to be added --->
During the mission to [[the Professor's castle]], Zhalia remained with an emotionally scarred Dante as the others went after [[the Professor]]. When the two found themselves under attack by [[Undergolem]] Titans invoked by [[Eathon the dog]], Zhalia's Titans were each swiftly defeated. After Dante came to his senses and defeated the Undergolem Titans, the two joined the fight against the Professor and his [[Legendary Titans]], eventually defeating him. {{source|The Mission}}

<!--- Details of adventures with the Foundation need to be added --->
[[File:S2E35 Dante Zhalia goodbye.png|thumb|170px|Zhalia and Dante say goodbye]]
Zhalia was left deeply troubled after being shown her future as a member of the [[Blood Spiral]] in a dreamworld created by [[Arc]], the Legendary Titan of Fate. {{source|The Legendary Titan of Fate}} After her plan to stop [[Kiel]], a [[Blood Spiral]] hunter failed, Zhalia realised that to beat the Spiral, she had to play to her strengths and become a spy and fight them from the inside. She left the Huntik team and said a tearful goodbye to Dante, giving him the [[Logosbook]] to keep in contact. {{source|Zhalia's Mission}}

After impressing [[Tantras]] with her loyalty, she was assigned as a personal bodyguard to [[Harrison Fears]]. {{source|Boys Will Be Seekers}} Over time, she grew attached to Harrison not only due to her mission, but also because of her liking towards him, becoming an older sister figure to him. {{source|Lok and the Betrayer}}

While undercover, she used a special diary to keep in contact with Dante through the [[Logosbook]] spell. When she wrote in her diary, the message was transmitted to Dante's copy of the diary, thus updating the team and the Huntik Foundation about the Blood Spiral's plans. When Tantras took her Logosbook, he noticed that she reported to Dante and commented that she must care for him very much. {{Source|Sophie on Trial}}
[[File:S2E51 Zhalia cry.png|thumb|170px|Zhalia breaks down after Dante's death]]

When [[the Betrayer]] revealed Dante's apparent death, she became devastated, dropping her disguise and openly revealing her alliance to the Foundation. {{source|Lok and the Betrayer}} Although she had previously received a message from Dante saying that they wouldn't be rid of him so easily, she was still shocked when he came back to life by using [[Copykind]] on [[Phoenix|Phoenix's]] Rebirth ability. After the Betrayer was finally defeated, she returned to the Huntik team, now led by Lok, with Dante having now joined the [[Huntik Foundation Council]]. {{source|Dante's Return}}

[[File:S1E24 Zhalia.png|thumb|200px]]
Despite being an expert at infiltration and spying, Zhalia sometimes has trouble masking her anxiety, as evidenced several times leading up to her exposure by [[Klaus]] and her subsequent redemption. {{source|The Vampire Loses Its Fangs}} She does not like being pushed around and will do things the way she wants most of the time. Zhalia tries to act strong and tough, but within she was weak until Dante showed her the way. {{source|The Mission}}

Zhalia's crush on team-member [[Dante Vale]] began during the mission to recover [[King Basilisk]], who would become one of Zhalia's principle Titans. {{source|Absent Heroes}} Dante was the first person in her life she felt expressed trust in her, choosing her to deliver the [[Hoplite]] Amulets recovered from the sunken [[Argo]]. {{source|Like Father, Unlike Son}} Due to this trust, Dante meant more to her that anything else in the world. {{source|The Divine Comedy}}

Zhalia also has a strong connection to the Fears brothers, especially Harrison. The two brothers come from the orphanage Zhalia lived in before the Organization, and their situation with the Blood Spiral is very similar to her experience with the Organization. During Zhalia's undercover mission, she was Harrison's bodyguard. This gave her access to information known only to higher-ups and a special relationship with Harrison. Harrison once said that she "was like a sister," suggesting that her bond with him wasn't just out of duty to her mission. Zhalia also had a rivalry with Sophie until the Professor's defeat, where Lok noted they're getting along better. {{source|S2E27}}

[[File:S2E52 Zhalia Dante.png|190px|thumb|Zhalia and Dante finally reunited after the war with [[the Betrayer]]]]
Zhalia and Dante had heard of one another as Foundation Seekers, and had a lot of respect for each other's skills, with Dante inviting her to help the Huntik team in Prague after their first meeting. {{Source|S1E03}} While other members of his team, particularly [[Sophie Casterwill]], took a distrust to Zhalia, Dante saw her as reliable and trustworthy, and let her prove herself to the team by rescuing [[Peter]] in Rouen. {{Source|S1E04}} Dante assured Zhalia that he trusted her after asking her to deliver [[DeFoe]]'s Amulets which meant a great deal to her as nobody had ever told her that. {{Source|S1E10}}  Over time, the pair began to develop feelings for one another {{Source|S1E17}}, and despite Zhalia's betrayal of his team to [[Klaus]], Dante understood her reasons and forgave her. {{Source|S1E17}} After the explosion at her [[Zhalia Moon's apartment|apartment]], the pair almost kissed but were interrupted by [[Lok Lambert]]. {{source|The Unseen Guide}} They grew deeply protective of one another {{Source|S1E23}} {{source|S2E27}} and Zhalia later admitted that Dante meant more to her than anything else in the world. {{source|S1E25}} 

When Zhalia chose to leave the team to infiltrate the [[Blood Spiral]], Dante was deeply saddened but understood why she had to go. {{Source|S2E35}} They stayed in touch by writing in a pair of [[Logosbook]] journals {{source|S2E36}} from which even [[Tantras]] could tell Zhalia cared for him a great deal. {{Source|S2E39}} When Zhalia discovered Dante had sacrificed himself to stop the [[Red Comet]], she was devastated. {{Source|S2E51}} However, Dante had written her a final message revealing his ultimate secret plan, and Zhalia was overjoyed to see him rise from the ashes. {{Source|S2E52}}

